<title>JAPAN: Thailand mulling 5-year, 10-year samurais -- sources.</title>
<headline>Thailand mulling 5-year, 10-year samurais -- sources.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand is considering offering 30 billion yen worth of samurai bonds in two tranches with five- and 10-year maturities by the end of the year, underwriting sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The Thai government is getting ready to select a lead manager,&quot; an underwriter said. &quot;It has been asking Japanese securities houses to gather information about the market.&quot;</p>
<p>In late October, the Thai government said it was planning to float two samurai bonds worth a total of 30 billion yen between November 15 and December 15 to raise funds for aircraft purchases by Thai Airways International Plc.</p>
</text>
